// What the product knows about one figure's history (CLEAN-261). One row per
// recorded figure in the registry (`domain/figures/`), written once, the
// first time the figure is seen at boot: the earliest row of its table, or
// that boot when the table is still empty. It is never moved later. A period
// view that starts before `completeSince` carries a note, so a block says
// "counted since …" instead of showing a smaller number as if it were the
// whole period (spec 038, FR-028).
//
// A figure read in place has no row here and never carries a note
// (CLEAN-262): its rows are the source, so no rows before some day means
// nothing happened before that day, not that something was missed. A row an
// earlier release wrote for one is removed at boot.
model StatFigure {
  key           String   @id
  completeSince DateTime
  updatedAt     DateTime @updatedAt
}
